{# narrative_engine/plot_obtain — how an item a planned step needs is got.
   Asked by PlotPlanning::Plan when a step needs an item nobody holds and
   it could be either stolen or bought. Whoever it is got from is decided
   afterwards. The answer is steal or buy.
   Receives: mastermind { name, standing }, bio, ambition, scheme, finish,
     history [{ step, outcome }], plan [step], need { step (its number in
     plan), sketch (that step), item }, options [{ key, step }]. Steps are
     records, worded by plot_step and plot_done.
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state who ]
{{ mastermind.name }}{% if length(mastermind.standing) > 0 %}, {% set standing = mastermind.standing %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_standing.prompt" %}{% endif %}.
{{ bio.summary }}
[ end state ]

[ state aims ]
The scheme: {{ scheme }}{% if length(finish) > 0 %}
It is meant to end with this: {{ finish }}{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state plan ]
{% for s in plan %}{{ loop.index1 }}. {% set step = s %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_step.prompt" %}
{% endfor %}[ end state ]

[ state need ]
Step {{ need.step }} needs {{ need.item }} in hand first: {% set step = need.sketch %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_step.prompt" %}
[ end state ]

[ question obtain choice ]
How does `who` get {{ need.item }} for the step in `need`, given the kind of person they are and what the scheme in `aims` is?
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {% set step = o.step %}{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_step.prompt" %}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
